<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'"><meta name="ca-artifact-format" content="codearbiter.artifact/0.1.0"><title>Last Stand playable loop · codeArbiter</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#172332;--muted:#516173;--line:#d5dde5;--paper:#fff;--soft:#f4f6f9;--accent:#81530b;--nav:#101923;--gold:#efba4a;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}html{scroll-behavior:auto;scroll-padding-top:1rem}body{margin:0;background:var(--soft);color:var(--ink);overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#235a86;text-decoration-thickness:.08em;text-underline-offset:.16em}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b36b00;outline-offset:4px}a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.skip{position:absolute;left:1rem;top:-8rem;z-index:5;background:white;padding:1rem}.skip:focus{top:1rem}.layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:17rem minmax(0,1fr);max-width:112rem;margin:auto}.sidebar{background:var(--nav);color:#dbe4ee;padding:2rem 1.5rem;position:sticky;top:0;height:100vh;overflow:auto}.sidebar img{max-width:100%;height:40px;width:auto;object-fit:contain;object-position:left}.sidebar h2{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b3c2d1;margin-top:2rem}.sidebar a{display:block;color:#dbe4ee;padding:.4rem 0;text-decoration:none;font-size:.9rem}.sidebar a:hover{color:var(--gold)}.sidebar p{font-size:.8rem;color:#aebdcc}.sidebar .companion{border-top:1px solid #3a4654;margin-top:1.5rem;padding-top:1.5rem}.main{padding:3rem clamp(1rem,4vw,5rem);max-width:90rem}.hero{padding-bottom:2rem;border-bottom:3px solid #26374a;margin-bottom:2rem}.eyebrow{font-size:.76rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700}.status{display:inline-block;font-size:.77rem;font-weight:700;background:#ece6db;color:#624513;padding:.3rem .65rem;border:1px solid #cec2ae;border-radius:.3rem}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:1.2rem 0}.deck{font-size:1.1rem;max-width:75ch}.meta{display:flex;gap:.6rem 1.2rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}h2{font-size:1.6rem;line-height:1.3}h3{font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.35}.group{margin:2.5rem 0}.group>h2{padding-bottom:.65rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.record{padding:1.5rem;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:.5rem;margin:1rem 0;box-shadow:0 1px 2px #17233205}.record .record{box-shadow:none;background:var(--soft);padding:1rem}.record-head{display:flex;gap:.65rem;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:.85rem}.record-head h3{margin:0;flex:1 1 20rem}.id{font:700 .78rem/1.5 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;color:#654f28;text-decoration:none;background:#f1ece0;border-radius:.2rem;padding:.15rem .4rem}.kind,.badge{font-size:.73rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--muted)}.retired{border-style:dashed;background:#f7f7f7}.field{margin:.9rem 0}.label{display:block;font-size:.76rem;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.25rem}.field p{margin:.2rem 0;white-space:pre-wrap}.missing{font-size:.9rem;color:#765810;font-style:italic}.items{padding-left:1.4rem;margin:.4rem 0}.items li{margin:.4rem 0}.fields{border-left:2px solid var(--line);padding-left:1rem}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;max-width:100%;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:.3rem;margin:1rem 0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem;table-layout:fixed}th,td{padding:.7rem .8rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);overflow-wrap:anywhere}th{background:#e9eef3;font-weight:700}tr:last-child td{border:0}pre{padding:1rem;background:#edf1f5;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:.3rem;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:.84rem/1.6 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace}code{font-family:ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace}.refs{font-size:.82rem;display:flex;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.block{margin:.8rem 0}.block p{white-space:pre-wrap}.notice{border-left:4px solid #a37825;padding:.8rem 1rem;background:#f4eddc}.footer{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1rem;margin-top:3rem}.digest{font: .75rem/1.6 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;word-break:break-all}details{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:.3rem;padding:.7rem 1rem}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.back{font-size:.8rem;float:right;margin-left:1rem}.record:target{outline:3px solid #b5812a;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:850px){.layout{display:block}.sidebar{position:relative;height:auto;padding:1.2rem 1rem}.sidebar nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.1rem 1rem}.sidebar nav a{padding:.2rem 0}.sidebar h2,.sidebar .identity{display:none}.sidebar .companion{margin-top:.7rem;padding-top:.7rem}.main{padding:1.5rem 1rem}.record{padding:1rem}.hero h1{font-size:2rem}table{font-size:.82rem}.record-head h3{flex-basis:100%}}@media print{.layout{display:block}.sidebar,.skip,.back{display:none}.main{max-width:none;padding:0}.record{box-shadow:none;break-inside:avoid;border-color:#888}.record .record{break-inside:auto}.hero h1{font-size:26pt}.group{break-before:auto}.group>h2{break-after:avoid}a{color:inherit}.table-wrap{overflow:visible}body{font-size:10pt;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}details{display:block}.footer{font-size:8pt}}
</style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main-content">Skip to document</a><div class="layout"><aside class="sidebar"><img src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," alt="codeArbiter"><p class="identity">ST-LS-LOOP-SPEC</p><h2>In this document</h2><nav aria-label="Document sections"><a href="#group-intent">Intent</a><a href="#group-scope">Scope</a><a href="#group-non_goals">Non goals</a><a href="#group-approach">Approach</a><a href="#group-constraints">Constraints</a><a href="#group-decisions">Decisions</a><a href="#group-criteria">Criteria</a><a href="#group-open_decisions">Open decisions</a><a href="#group-sections">Sections</a><a href="#group-sources">Sources</a><a href="#group-baseline">Baseline</a><a href="#group-retired_symbols">Retired symbols</a></nav><a class="companion" href="../plans/last-stand-playable-loop.html">Open companion implementation plan</a><p>Generated from the embedded model. Edit through the artifact engine, not the HTML view.</p></aside><main class="main" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">codeArbiter / spec</p><span class="status">DRAFT · authority must be verified at use</span><h1>Last Stand playable loop</h1><p class="deck">A dedicated local prototype: fight, defeat, claim salvage, buy permanent Cannon Attack, and redeploy with a visible combat improvement. Build direction and prototype values are proposed for this pair; owner art acceptance remains separate.</p><div class="meta"><span>ST-LS-LOOP-SPEC</span><span>Revision 2 · schema 0.3.1</span><span>30 addressable records</span></div></header><section class="group" id="group-intent"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Intent</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:INTENT-01 -->
<article class="record" id="INTENT-01" data-ca-symbol="INTENT-01" data-ca-kind="intent"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#INTENT-01">INTENT-01</a><h3>Intent</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Caller</span>Owner building Last Stand in the Unity Web prototype</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Outcome</span>A player can deploy, reach ordinary defeat, claim exactly one salvage, buy Cannon Attack, reload on the same origin, and redeploy with a clearly stronger cannon in a coherent interface with original sound feedback.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Problem</span>The existing encounter and pure shop fixture do not yet deliver an awarding, saved, playable upgrade loop.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li><li><a href="#SRC-02">SRC-02</a></li></ul></div></article>
<!-- CA:END:INTENT-01 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-scope"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Scope</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:SCOPE-01 -->
<article class="record" id="SCOPE-01" data-ca-symbol="SCOPE-01" data-ca-kind="scope"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#SCOPE-01">SCOPE-01</a><h3>Scope</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Defeat reward and capped permanent Cannon Attack with real next-run damage.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:SCOPE-01 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:SCOPE-02 -->
<article class="record" id="SCOPE-02" data-ca-symbol="SCOPE-02" data-ca-kind="scope"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#SCOPE-02">SCOPE-02</a><h3>Scope</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Versioned local save, idempotent Claim, failure/retry, and same-origin reload.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:SCOPE-02 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:SCOPE-03 -->
<article class="record" id="SCOPE-03" data-ca-symbol="SCOPE-03" data-ca-kind="scope"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#SCOPE-03">SCOPE-03</a><h3>Scope</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Dedicated gameplay scene, coherent garage/battle/results/workshop flow, compact layout, and original sound feedback.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:SCOPE-03 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:SCOPE-04 -->
<article class="record" id="SCOPE-04" data-ca-symbol="SCOPE-04" data-ca-kind="scope"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#SCOPE-04">SCOPE-04</a><h3>Scope</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Preserve review/legacy behavior and prove the bounded real loop through actual C#, Unity, and browser execution.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:SCOPE-04 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-non_goals"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Non goals</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:NON-GOAL-01 -->
<article class="record" id="NON-GOAL-01" data-ca-symbol="NON-GOAL-01" data-ca-kind="non_goals"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#NON-GOAL-01">NON-GOAL-01</a><h3>Non goals</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>No owner art selection, live-player session, merge, deployment, account/backend/cloud save, multi-tab economy authority, mobile certification, final balance, new enemies/weapons, in-run shop integration, music, middleware, or new test framework.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:NON-GOAL-01 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-approach"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Approach</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:APPROACH-01 -->
<article class="record" id="APPROACH-01" data-ca-symbol="APPROACH-01" data-ca-kind="approach"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#APPROACH-01">APPROACH-01</a><h3>Approach</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Binding decision refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#DEC-01">DEC-01</a></li><li><a href="#DEC-02">DEC-02</a></li><li><a href="#DEC-03">DEC-03</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Choice</span>Use a dedicated LastStandPrototype scene copied from the existing battlefield scene, a scene-local loop controller, pure progression state, a tiny localStorage bridge, and the existing session/art owners.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Tradeoff</span>A local single-tab prototype demonstrates the real loop quickly. It does not promise cloud accounts, authoritative rewards, cross-origin persistence, multi-tab atomicity, or final balance.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:APPROACH-01 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-constraints"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Constraints</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:CONSTRAINT-01 -->
<article class="record" id="CONSTRAINT-01" data-ca-symbol="CONSTRAINT-01" data-ca-kind="constraints"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#CONSTRAINT-01">CONSTRAINT-01</a><h3>Constraints</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applies to</span><ul class="items"><li>SCOPE-01</li><li>SCOPE-02</li><li>SCOPE-03</li><li>SCOPE-04</li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li><li><a href="#SRC-02">SRC-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Preserve the owner A/B keep/change/mix and normal-speed visual acceptance gates, the no-merge instruction, and remote live-player deferral. Draft readiness and automated evidence do not satisfy those gates.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:CONSTRAINT-01 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:CONSTRAINT-02 -->
<article class="record" id="CONSTRAINT-02" data-ca-symbol="CONSTRAINT-02" data-ca-kind="constraints"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#CONSTRAINT-02">CONSTRAINT-02</a><h3>Constraints</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applies to</span><ul class="items"><li>SCOPE-01</li><li>SCOPE-02</li><li>SCOPE-03</li><li>SCOPE-04</li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-02">SRC-02</a></li><li><a href="#SRC-03">SRC-03</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>All new awards are forgeable local prototype state only. Do not touch classic-client account progression, Supabase, SQL, credentials, verified awards, the existing MechanicsShopModel contract, or old native artifact records. No runtime dependency or broad verification framework.</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:CONSTRAINT-02 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-decisions"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Decisions</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:DEC-01 -->
<article class="record" id="DEC-01" data-ca-symbol="DEC-01" data-ca-kind="decisions"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#DEC-01">DEC-01</a><h3>Build order and owner gates</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Authority</span>proposed</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Choice</span>Build the dedicated playable loop now while A/B still choice and normal-speed motion acceptance remain pending; do not merge PR 524 until owner acceptance.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>The owner explicitly wants a practical polished loop next. Building this new mode does not select an art treatment or claim acceptance of existing alternatives.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source ref</span><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></div></article>
<!-- CA:END:DEC-01 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:DEC-02 -->
<article class="record" id="DEC-02" data-ca-symbol="DEC-02" data-ca-kind="decisions"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#DEC-02">DEC-02</a><h3>Reversible prototype economy</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Authority</span>proposed</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Choice</span>Cannon Attack levels 0..3 deal 20/30/40/50 cannon damage. Each ordinary defeat offers 1 salvage; next permanent level costs 1/2/3 salvage. Initial wallet and level are zero.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>The first upgrade visibly changes a 30 HP first foe from surviving at 10 HP to a one-hit cannon defeat. Three capped levels avoid a one-purchase dead end without introducing an upgrade catalog. This is independent of fixture-only in-run C(n+1) shop pricing.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source ref</span><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></div></article>
<!-- CA:END:DEC-02 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:DEC-03 -->
<article class="record" id="DEC-03" data-ca-symbol="DEC-03" data-ca-kind="decisions"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#DEC-03">DEC-03</a><h3>Dedicated mode and save boundary</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Authority</span>proposed</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Choice</span>Use profile playable-prototype-v1 with an explicit copy of provisional review pacing, a local version-1 JSON save, and original procedural SFX. Preserve the non-awarding review scene and legacy encounter.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>Reuses art and established timing without silently changing review mechanics or adding a backend, audio middleware, save framework, or dependency.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source ref</span><a href="#SRC-03">SRC-03</a></div></article>
<!-- CA:END:DEC-03 -->
</section><section class="group" id="group-criteria"><a class="back" href="#main-content">Top</a><h2>Criteria</h2>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:AC-01 -->
<article class="record" id="AC-01" data-ca-symbol="AC-01" data-ca-kind="criteria"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#AC-01">AC-01</a><h3>One defeat, one reward</h3><span class="badge">must</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applicability</span><div class="fields"><div class="field"><span class="label">Mode</span>unconditional</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>Required for the bounded playable prototype loop.</div></div></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Constraint refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-01">CONSTRAINT-01</a></li><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-02">CONSTRAINT-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Intent refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SCOPE-01">SCOPE-01</a></li><li><a href="#SCOPE-04">SCOPE-04</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Kind</span>behavior</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Scenarios</span><span class="missing">None recorded</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Only ordinary Defeated in gameplay mode produces a staged 1-salvage reward. Capture terminal time/kills before releasing the model. Claim is idempotent, and abandon, pause, focus loss, technical failure and non-defeat horizon award zero. Each fitting can reach ordinary defeat under playable-prototype-v1.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Verification</span>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:VERIFY-01 -->
<article class="record" id="VERIFY-01" data-ca-symbol="VERIFY-01" data-ca-kind="verification"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#VERIFY-01">VERIFY-01</a><h3>Verification</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Evidence state</span>planned</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Method</span>automated_and_review</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Negative control</span>A duplicate Claim or failure transition that grants salvage fails the focused case.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Oracle</span>Repeated terminal/Claim input leaves exactly one credit; excluded outcomes leave wallet unchanged; both fittings terminate as Defeated.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Planned target</span>Compiled progression cases and real Unity lifecycle check</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:VERIFY-01 -->
</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:AC-01 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:AC-02 -->
<article class="record" id="AC-02" data-ca-symbol="AC-02" data-ca-kind="criteria"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#AC-02">AC-02</a><h3>Save before economic success</h3><span class="badge">must</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applicability</span><div class="fields"><div class="field"><span class="label">Mode</span>unconditional</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>Required for the bounded playable prototype loop.</div></div></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Constraint refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-01">CONSTRAINT-01</a></li><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-02">CONSTRAINT-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Intent refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SCOPE-02">SCOPE-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Kind</span>behavior</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Scenarios</span><span class="missing">None recorded</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Use the versioned single JSON object and save/retry contract in SEC-01. Deployment, claim and purchase become successful only after exact localStorage readback. Restore saved pending reward and purchased level on same-origin reload. Reject malformed/version/shape/ID state without erasing it or enabling purchases.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Verification</span>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:VERIFY-02 -->
<article class="record" id="VERIFY-02" data-ca-symbol="VERIFY-02" data-ca-kind="verification"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#VERIFY-02">VERIFY-02</a><h3>Verification</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Evidence state</span>planned</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Method</span>automated_and_review</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Negative control</span>Throwing getter/setter, mismatched readback, write-then-read failure and malformed save each refuse false success.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Oracle</span>Failed get/set/readback preserves committed wallet/level and disables economic transitions; retry safely reconciles an uncertain successful write; reload preserves one pending or claimed reward without duplication.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Planned target</span>Compiled save-transition cases, actual WebGL bridge and real-browser reload</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:VERIFY-02 -->
</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:AC-02 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:AC-03 -->
<article class="record" id="AC-03" data-ca-symbol="AC-03" data-ca-kind="criteria"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#AC-03">AC-03</a><h3>Upgrade changes real next-run combat</h3><span class="badge">must</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applicability</span><div class="fields"><div class="field"><span class="label">Mode</span>unconditional</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>Required for the bounded playable prototype loop.</div></div></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Constraint refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-01">CONSTRAINT-01</a></li><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-02">CONSTRAINT-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Intent refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SCOPE-01">SCOPE-01</a></li><li><a href="#SCOPE-04">SCOPE-04</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Kind</span>behavior</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Scenarios</span><span class="missing">None recorded</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Cannon Attack level 0..3 uses damage 20/30/40/50 and permanent costs 1/2/3. Insufficient funds and cap refuse without mutation; purchases occur outside combat and apply on the next Deploy. With the same repair fitting and gameplay profile, the first 30 HP foe has 10 HP after one baseline cannon hit and is defeated by one level-1 cannon hit.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Verification</span>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:VERIFY-03 -->
<article class="record" id="VERIFY-03" data-ca-symbol="VERIFY-03" data-ca-kind="verification"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#VERIFY-03">VERIFY-03</a><h3>Verification</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Evidence state</span>planned</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Method</span>automated_and_review</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Negative control</span>A cosmetic-only damage label, changed fitting/profile, charge on cap, or live mid-run upgrade fails.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Oracle</span>Real EncounterModel damage and visible combat outcome agree with garage/workshop/battle damage labels; active run loadout/damage remain frozen.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Planned target</span>Actual C# model and imported Unity session, corroborated by normal-speed browser loop</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:VERIFY-03 -->
</div></article>
<!-- CA:END:AC-03 -->

<!-- CA:BEGIN:AC-04 -->
<article class="record" id="AC-04" data-ca-symbol="AC-04" data-ca-kind="criteria"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#AC-04">AC-04</a><h3>Clear compact player loop</h3><span class="badge">must</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Applicability</span><div class="fields"><div class="field"><span class="label">Mode</span>unconditional</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Rationale</span>Required for the bounded playable prototype loop.</div></div></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Constraint refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-01">CONSTRAINT-01</a></li><li><a href="#CONSTRAINT-02">CONSTRAINT-02</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Intent refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SCOPE-03">SCOPE-03</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Kind</span>behavior</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Scenarios</span><span class="missing">None recorded</span></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Source refs</span><ul class="items"><li><a href="#SRC-01">SRC-01</a></li></ul></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Statement</span>Provide the SEC-02 garage, battle, results and one-card workshop flow using one existing session and Canvas. Display truthful saved-state/failure/retry, balance, price and current -&gt; next damage. Keep the action visible at 800x600, and label the dedicated Web entry Last Stand.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Verification</span>
<!-- CA:BEGIN:VERIFY-04 -->
<article class="record" id="VERIFY-04" data-ca-symbol="VERIFY-04" data-ca-kind="verification"><div class="record-head"><a class="id" href="#VERIFY-04">VERIFY-04</a><h3>Verification</h3></div><div class="field"><span class="label">Evidence state</span>planned</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Method</span>automated_and_review</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Negative control</span>A compact hidden CTA or failed-storage success label prevents a passing browser result.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Oracle</span>No overlapping phase controls, duplicate Canvas/session, off-screen action, false Saved label or gameplay A/B/debug controls; pointer input completes Claim, Buy and Redeploy.</div><div class="field"><span class="label">Planned target</span>Real Unity hierarchy/lifecycle check and normal-speed browser pointer/capture proof at 1280x720 and 800x600</div></article>
