        "authority": "proposed",
        "choice": "Use profile playable-prototype-v1 with an explicit copy of provisional review pacing, a local version-1 JSON save, and original procedural SFX. Preserve the non-awarding review scene and legacy encounter.",
        "id": "DEC-03",
        "rationale": "Reuses art and established timing without silently changing review mechanics or adding a backend, audio middleware, save framework, or dependency.",
        "source_ref": "SRC-03",
        "topic": "Dedicated mode and save boundary"
      }
    ],
    "governs": [],
    "intent": {
      "caller": "Owner building Last Stand in the Unity Web prototype",
      "id": "INTENT-01",
      "outcome": "A player can deploy, reach ordinary defeat, claim exactly one salvage, buy Cannon Attack, reload on the same origin, and redeploy with a clearly stronger cannon in a coherent interface with original sound feedback.",
      "problem": "The existing encounter and pure shop fixture do not yet deliver an awarding, saved, playable upgrade loop.",
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC-01",
        "SRC-02"
      ]
    },
    "non_goals": [
      {
        "id": "NON-GOAL-01",
        "statement": "No owner art selection, live-player session, merge, deployment, account/backend/cloud save, multi-tab economy authority, mobile certification, final balance, new enemies/weapons, in-run shop integration, music, middleware, or new test framework."
      }
    ],
    "open_decisions": [],
    "retired_symbols": [],
    "scope": [
      {
        "id": "SCOPE-01",
        "statement": "Defeat reward and capped permanent Cannon Attack with real next-run damage."
      },
      {
        "id": "SCOPE-02",
        "statement": "Versioned local save, idempotent Claim, failure/retry, and same-origin reload."
      },
      {
        "id": "SCOPE-03",
        "statement": "Dedicated gameplay scene, coherent garage/battle/results/workshop flow, compact layout, and original sound feedback."
      },
      {
        "id": "SCOPE-04",
        "statement": "Preserve review/legacy behavior and prove the bounded real loop through actual C#, Unity, and browser execution."
      }
    ],
    "sections": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "refs": [],
            "text": "Store one JSON object under singedTerra.lastStand.prototype.v1: version=1, nonnegative integral credits, permanentLevel 0..3, monotonic nextRunId, lastFinalizedRunId, and optional pendingDefeat containing runId, reward=1, elapsedTicks and kills. Reserve and persist a new run ID before Deploy. Capture ordinary defeat metrics before ReturnToInspection releases the model, and persist the pending reward before enabling Claim. Claim atomically clears pendingDefeat, adds one credit, and records the finalized run ID in one write. Purchase atomically subtracts its exact cost and increments the level in one write. Commit in-memory economic state only after setItem and exact readback succeed. Exact duplicate callbacks/claims do not award twice. A lost active run on reload is abandoned without reward; a saved pending defeat restores the claim flow. A missing record initializes zero state through a successful write; malformed, unsupported-version or inconsistent saved data is preserved and blocks economic transitions with an explanation and Retry. Storage failure preserves current committed state and pending operation; Retry reconciles a matching already-written candidate before retrying so a write followed by failed readback cannot duplicate rewards. Do not silently replace durable storage with memory or auto-reset corrupt data. No claim of crash-proof disk persistence or concurrent-tab atomicity.",
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "id": "SEC-01",
        "title": "Save and failure contract"
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "refs": [],
            "text": "Garage has fitting, permanent level, cannon damage and next benefit, saved-state text and Deploy. Battle shows hull, elapsed time, kills, current cannon damage, pause and mute. Ordinary defeat lets final recoil/impact effects settle for a short bounded transition, then presents time, kills, reward, balance and Claim and Continue. Workshop has one Cannon Attack card with current -\u003e next damage, cost, balance, insufficient/capped/disabled states, purchase confirmation and Redeploy. Results/workshop replace nonessential battle and review controls; at 800x600 the primary action stays visible and reachable. No A/B selector, recoil-preview, orbit or part-debug controls in gameplay mode. Original procedural cannon, impact/destruction, defeat and purchase cues use bounded overlapping AudioSources, unlock from Deploy, stop while paused/hidden and obey a visible mute retained for the current session. No deferred audio burst on resume. Web title/loading identify Last Stand.",
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "id": "SEC-02",
        "title": "Player flow and feedback"
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "refs": [],
            "text": "Use focused actual C# compiler cases, one real Unity Editor lifecycle/combat/scene check, and one source-bound Web export plus a bounded real-pointer loop at normal speed. Browser proof includes same-origin reload, saved pending reward and post-purchase state, plus compact layout and audio/mute/pause inspection. Existing early-tick review smoke alone is insufficient for this loop. Do not claim numeric C# coverage: Unity/C# is unmentioned in the repository Testing profile and no configured numeric coverage runner exists. Preserve source and saved review/legacy scene hashes. Owner visual acceptance and live-player feedback remain explicitly pending.",
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "id": "SEC-03",
        "title": "Verification boundaries"
      }
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
